# The website: `site/` holds only the Hugo configuration. The pages, Hugo's
# caches and the rendered output are all built.
#
# `/site/content/` is the site build's output root (`site.out` in
# package-build.config.yaml). It is wiped on every run, so nothing in it is
# authored — the homepage it holds is generated from
# `assets/content/homepage.md`. The rendered HTML goes to
# `build/site/harnensemble/`, not to Hugo's default `public/`, so the deployed
# tree carries its own prefix; `/site/public/` is listed anyway so a stray
# `hugo` run without `--source`'s configuration cannot be committed.
/site/content/
/site/public/
/site/resources/
/site/.hugo_build.lock
# Legacy: the compiled LevelDB packs landed at the repository root until the
# packs moved into the build stage (#26). Kept so a checkout that still carries
# the old directory does not report it as untracked.
/packs

